{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["The reason for <b>eleven days from Horeb</b>: Scripture informs us of the extent of the wilderness, for from Horeb, from which they set out, to Kadesh-barnea is a journey of only eleven days, for it is close by way of Mount Seir, and Kadesh-barnea is the end of the wilderness at the border of the hill country of the Amorites, which is the inheritance of Israel, and there is the land of Sihon and Og, where it says, \"across the Jordan, in the land of Moab, Moses undertook to expound this Torah\" (Deuteronomy 1:5) — in the valley opposite Beth-peor. And after that it says that they journeyed by way of the hill country of the Amorites, through all the great and terrible wilderness, and afterward it recounts that at Kadesh-barnea, which is within the boundary of their inheritance, they requested spies and their way became confounded, and they journeyed back toward the Red Sea, backward and not forward, until the completion of forty years. And because Israel were not now in the wilderness, for they had already entered the land of Moab which is mentioned, Onkelos interpreted <b>in the wilderness, in the Arabah</b> as an allusion to reproofs. Furthermore, why would Scripture mention all these places and give signs and markers more than one who surveys a field? And the measure of Scripture, according to his opinion, is for these things: \"These are the words that Moses spoke to all Israel across the Jordan — in the wilderness, in the Arabah, opposite the Red Sea, between Paran and Tophel and Laban and Hazeroth and Di-zahab — eleven days from Horeb,\" for he recalled to them all that they had done in these places, and afterward Scripture says that there, across the Jordan mentioned, he undertook to expound the Torah after reproofing them, and he answered and said: \"YHWH our Elohim spoke to us in Horeb, saying\" (Deuteronomy 1:6). And so it is expounded in Sifrei (Deuteronomy 1) according to the opinion of Rabbi Judah. But Rabbi Jose ben Dormasqit made them places that were so named:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:43:58.195237650Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}